{
  "text": "What if editing a video felt like talking to a friend who is really good at it? You tell them what you want. They do the work. You say, make it a little faster, and it's done. That is Boss Studio. Boss Studio is an editing app powered by AI. You record the video. Boss does the editing, the cuts, the captions, the graphics, and the sound. Think of it as your own video editor who never gets tired and never says, I'm busy. Here is what Boss can do. It cleans up your talking. It finds the ums, the repeats, and the false starts and takes them out. It gives your video a look you pick from a selection of styles. Choosing one is like choosing an outfit. It adds captions that pop, moving words, cards, and graphics. It adds music and sound effects too. And it makes the right shape for where you post, tall for Reels and TikTok, wide for YouTube. The best part? You stay the boss. Nothing is final until you say so. Let's take a quick tour. This is the projects page. Every project gets its own folder on your computer so your videos stay private. Start a project click new project give it a name add your raw video write your first idea in your own words Then pick a style you have two ways to go Press create project to review each step yourself or press magic edit and boss decides everything and shows you the result when it's done Step one script boss listens to your video and writes down every word now You can read your video like a document select any words You don't want and delete them or press suggest cleanup and boss finds the stutters and retakes for you. Press preview edits to watch it with those parts skipped. Your original video is never changed. Step two, instructions. Tell boss what you want in plain words. For example, make it energetic with big captions. You can tick boxes to clean up the sound, add soft music or add sound effects. You can even paste a video you like and Boss will copy its style. Step three, editing. Boss gets to work. A progress bar shows you it's busy. When it's done, you get a fast, small draft to review. Watch the draft. Switch between the script and the frames to jump anywhere in the video. See something to change? Pause and press snapshot. The frame opens big and you can draw right on it. Circle it. Point an arrow at it. Then write a note like, make this word bigger and add a pop sound. Each note sticks to that exact second. Add as many as you want, and when you have your notes, press Render Draft and Boss fixes everything in one go. Step four, Gallery. Every version is saved so you can compare them. Open any of them, show the file in its folder, or send it to Google Drive with one click. Drafts are small, so they're fast. When you love one, press Render Final Version. That makes the full quality video. That's it. Start, Script, Instructions, Editing, Gallery. You don't need to be an editor. You just need to know what you want. Boss Studio, your vision. boss does the editing start creating",
